{
  "_comment": [
    "Twenty-two packed bags, described as data rather than built by the packing",
    "engine.",
    "",
    "Deliberately not run through `buildPackingList`, for the reason",
    "`tests/packing-memo-deterministic.test.ts` gives: this scores the MEMO, and a",
    "score that moved because the beam search drifted would be a measurement about",
    "the wrong module. Every scenario states its own looks, pieces and shortfall,",
    "so the memo has exactly one input and the scorer can recompute the expected",
    "counts independently.",
    "",
    "`forecasts` are [lowC, highC, precipitationChance] triples, one per day.",
    "`looks[].items` of null is a look the closet could not fill — the shortfall",
    "the memo has to name honestly rather than round away.",
    "",
    "Coverage is chosen to hit every branch the memo has: an empty bag, a",
    "single-piece bag, one night and seven, all four day parts, rain with and",
    "without outerwear in the bag, a worn-on-the-plane piece, normals standing in",
    "for a forecast, and both unit systems."
  ],
